%% Title: Batch Aggregate Seal Write Commit Failure Lifecycle
%% @version 1.1.0
%% @date    2026-10-09
%% Reviewed against main 9a7339dc: domain/aggregates/_batch_aggregate.py and batch.py
%% @type    stateDiagram
%% @level   Domain / Aggregate
%% @nodes   5
%% RULES: RULES.md §2.1, ADR-021
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> OPEN
    OPEN --> OPEN: add_record()
    OPEN --> SEALED: seal / seal_with_counts
    SEALED --> WRITING: mark_writing()
    WRITING --> COMMITTED: mark_committed(layer, committed_at)
    WRITING --> FAILED: mark_failed(layer, error, failed_at)
    COMMITTED --> [*]
    FAILED --> [*]

    note right of OPEN
      Batch intake remains mutable until the aggregate is sealed.
      Seal counts must be non-negative and satisfy
      valid_count + quarantined_count = record_count.
    end note

    note right of WRITING
      After mark_writing(), publisher paths should not mutate logical batch content.
    end note
